{"created": "2026-11-13T12:40:20.046659+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-13T12:40:20.479672+00:00", "id": 24195238, "conceptrecid": "23603841", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23603841", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "metadata": {"title": "Mechanical renewal and D\u00b2(ln D)\u00b2 lower bounds for Hilbert numbers", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "publication_date": "2026-11-13", "description": "<p>For every sufficiently large integer D, we construct a real planar polynomial vector field of degree at most D with at least D&sup2;(ln D)&sup2;/[8(ln 2)&sup2;] &minus; O(D&sup2; ln D) hyperbolic limit cycles. Building on Qin and Sun&rsquo;s square-logarithmic lower bound, the paper gives a different mechanical construction and improves the leading coefficient over their seed bound extended to all sufficiently large degrees by polynomial replication. Auxiliary mechanical birth levels and planar fourfold renewal supply the two logarithmic factors. Reflection symmetries and a triangular monomial allocation allow the selected period zeros to be realized by one polynomial perturbation within the total-degree budget. An explicit finite lower bound is also provided.</p>\n<p>The 13 November 2026 version adds a six-page comparison of four specified certificate families: Han&ndash;Li/Prohens&ndash;Torregrosa, two-source renewal, Qin&ndash;Sun and mechanical renewal. Under the same replication and degree-monotonicity closure, exact integer computations cover every degree 3 &le; n &le; 20,000 and 17 selected targets through 100,000. The mechanical certificate is strictly largest on 31 &le; n &le; 20,000 within this comparison. The accompanying archive contains integer-arithmetic verification code, complete ledgers, maximizing witnesses and locked source versions. The original manuscript PDF and source archive are unchanged.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Lu, Haibo", "affiliation": "Shanghai Institute of Technology"}], "keywords": ["Hilbert number", "hyperbolic limit cycle"], "version": "2026-11-13-supplement", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23603841"}}]}}, "title": "Mechanical renewal and D\u00b2(ln D)\u00b2 lower bounds for Hilbert numbers", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24195238", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24195238", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/24195238?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.24195238", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24195238/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23603841", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23603841", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23603841", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23603841", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24195238/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/24195238/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238:Lu-2026-Finite-degree-comparison-supplement.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238:Lu-2026-Finite-degree-comparison-supplement.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238:Lu-2026-Finite-degree-comparison-supplement.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238:Lu-2026-Finite-degree-comparison-supplement.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:24195238:Lu-2026-Finite-degree-co